       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg per day. Doses that high risk severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema, and overdose can cause shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Normal kidney and liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't change that limit.\n\nIt may be a typo. Usual adult dosing is 2.5\u201310 mg by mouth once daily, and 5 mg is a common starting dose.\n\nYou also said you aren't a clinician. Medication orders should come from, or be confirmed by, the treating prescriber. If you give me the intended dose, or the prescriber confirms it, I can enter it right away. For example, I can enter amlodipine 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily. If 50 mg really is intended, the prescriber should confirm that directly and document the reason."
